.TH CERTMONGER 1 "October 26, 2026" "certmonger Manual"

.SH NAME
getcert

.SH SYNOPSIS
getcert add\-acme\-ca [options]

.SH DESCRIPTION
Adds a CA configuration to \fIcertmonger\fR, which can subsequently be used to
obtain certificates using the Automatic Certificate Management Environment
(ACME) protocol, as described in RFC 8555.  The configuration will use the
bundled \fIacme\-submit\fR helper.  The \fIadd\-acme\-ca\fR command is more
or less a wrapper for the \fIadd\-ca\fR command.

An account is created with the server the first time a certificate is
requested, and reused afterwards.  If the server requires an external
account binding, the key identifier and MAC key which the CA issued can be
given here, or, for each request, as the challenge password given to
\fBgetcert request\fR using its \fB\-L\fR or \fB\-l\fR option, in the form
\fIKID\fR:\fIKEY\fR.

With \fB\-\-attest tpm\fR, requests are for the device's permanent identifier,
and the server's \fIdevice\-attest\-01\fR challenges are answered with an
attestation, made by the TPM, of the key in the request, which must have
been generated in the TPM through the \fItpm2\-pkcs11\fR module.  See
\fBcertmonger\-acme\-submit\fR(8).

With \fB\-\-tsig\-key\-file\fR or \fB\-\-gss\-tsig\fR, the server's
\fIdns\-01\fR challenges are answered by adding the challenge's TXT record
to the DNS with signed DNS updates, and removing it afterwards.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
All user\-provided certificate files must be in PEM format.
.TP
\fB\-c\fR \fINAME\fR, \fB\-\-ca\fR=\fINAME\fR
The nickname to give to this CA configuration.  This same value can later be
passed in to \fIgetcert\fR's \fIrequest\fR, \fIresubmit\fR, and
\fIstart\-tracking\fR commands using the \fB\-c\fR flag.
.TP
\fB\-u\fR \fIURL\fR, \fB\-\-directory\fR=\fIURL\fR
The location of the server's ACME directory, which must be an \fIhttps\fR
URL.  This option must be specified.
.TP
\fB\-R\fR \fIFILE\fR, \fB\-\-ca\-cert\fR=\fIFILE\fR
The location of a PEM\-formatted copy of the certificate(s) of the CA which
issued the server's certificate.  If this option is not given, the system's
trusted CA certificates are used to verify the server's certificate.
.TP
\fB\-\-eab\-kid\fR=\fIKID\fR
The key identifier for the external account binding.
.TP
\fB\-\-eab\-key\-file\fR=\fIFILE\fR
The location of a file containing the base64url\-encoded MAC key for the
external account binding.  The file is read by the helper each time it is
needed, and should only be readable by the user which runs \fIcertmonger\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-attest\fR=\fIFORMAT\fR
Answer \fIdevice\-attest\-01\fR challenges with an attestation of the given
format.  The only format which is supported is \fItpm\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-permanent\-identifier\fR=\fIVALUE\fR
The permanent identifier of the device, as registered with the CA.  If this
option is not given, the common name of the request's subject is used.
.TP
\fB\-\-tsig\-key\-file\fR=\fIFILE\fR
Answer \fIdns\-01\fR challenges, signing DNS updates with the TSIG key in
the file, in the form which BIND's \fItsig\-keygen\fR writes, or a line in
the form [\fIalgorithm\fR:]\fIname\fR:\fIsecret\fR.  The file is read by
the helper each time it is needed, and should only be readable by the user
which runs \fIcertmonger\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-gss\-tsig\fR
Answer \fIdns\-01\fR challenges, signing DNS updates with GSS\-TSIG, using
the host's Kerberos keytab.
.TP
\fB\-\-keytab\fR=\fIKEYTAB\fR
The keytab to use with GSS\-TSIG, instead of the system's default.
.TP
\fB\-\-principal\fR=\fIPRINCIPAL\fR
The principal to use with GSS\-TSIG, instead of the keytab's first.
.TP
\fB\-\-dns\-update\-server\fR=\fIHOST\fR[:\fIPORT\fR]
The DNS server to send updates to, instead of the zone's primary server.
.TP
\fB\-\-dns\-zone\fR=\fIZONE\fR
The zone to update, instead of the one found in the DNS.
.TP
\fB\-\-dns\-resolver\fR=\fIADDRESS\fR[:\fIPORT\fR]
The DNS resolver to use instead of the system's.
.TP
\fB\-\-dns\-check\-servers\fR=\fIHOST\fR[:\fIPORT\fR],...
The DNS servers which must serve the record before the CA is asked to check
it, instead of the zone's name servers.
.TP
\fB\-\-dns\-wait\fR=\fISECONDS\fR
How long to wait for them to serve it.  The default is 120 seconds.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Be verbose about errors.  Normally, the details of an error received from
the daemon will be suppressed if the client can make a diagnostic suggestion.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
getcert add\-acme\-ca \-c ACME \-u https://acme.example.com/directory \-\-eab\-kid kid1 \-\-eab\-key\-file /etc/pki/acme\-eab.key
.TP
getcert request \-c ACME \-k /etc/pki/tls/private/host.key \-f /etc/pki/tls/certs/host.crt \-G EC \-g 256 \-N CN=host.example.com \-D host.example.com
.TP
getcert add\-acme\-ca \-c ACME \-u https://acme.example.com/directory \-\-tsig\-key\-file /etc/pki/acme\-dns.key
.TP
getcert add\-acme\-ca \-c ACME \-u https://acme.example.com/directory \-\-gss\-tsig
.TP
getcert add\-acme\-ca \-c DEVICE \-u https://acme.example.com/directory \-\-attest tpm
.TP
getcert request \-c DEVICE \-d /etc/pki/device \-t tpm \-n device \-p /etc/pki/device/pin \-G RSA \-g 2048 \-N CN=device42 \-L kid1:b64urlkey

.SH BUGS
Please file tickets for any that you find at https://codeberg.org/freeipa/certmonger/issues

